{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1678","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B1. Tokitsukaze and Good 01-String (easy version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is the easy version of the problem. The only difference between the two versions is that the harder version asks additionally for a minimum number of subsegments."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tokitsukaze has a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting only of zeros and ones, $$$n$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"even"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Tokitsukaze divides $$$s$$$ into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the minimum number"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"contiguous"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" subsegments, and for each subsegment, all bits in each subsegment are the same. After that, $$$s$$$ is considered good if the lengths of all subsegments are even."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$s$$$ is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11001111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", it will be divided into \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Their lengths are $$$2$$$, $$$2$$$, $$$4$$$ respectively, which are all even numbers, so \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11001111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is good. Another example, if $$$s$$$ is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1110011000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", it will be divided into \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and their lengths are $$$3$$$, $$$2$$$, $$$2$$$, $$$3$$$. Obviously, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1110011000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is not good."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tokitsukaze wants to make $$$s$$$ good by changing the values of some positions in $$$s$$$. Specifically, she can perform the operation any number of times: change the value of $$$s_i$$$ to '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'($$$1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$). Can you tell her the minimum number of operations to make $$$s$$$ good?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first contains a single positive integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10\\,000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, the first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of $$$s$$$, it is guaranteed that $$$n$$$ is even."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a binary string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting only of zeros and ones."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single line with one integer — the minimum number of operations to make $$$s$$$ good."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n10\n1110011000\n8\n11001111\n2\n00\n2\n11\n6\n100110\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n0\n0\n0\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, one of the ways to make $$$s$$$ good is the following."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Change $$$s_3$$$, $$$s_6$$$ and $$$s_7$$$ to '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', after that $$$s$$$ becomes \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1100000000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", it can be divided into \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00000000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", which lengths are $$$2$$$ and $$$8$$$ respectively. There are other ways to operate $$$3$$$ times to make $$$s$$$ good, such as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1111110000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1100001100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1111001100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second, third and fourth test cases, $$$s$$$ is good initially, so no operation is required."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B1","problemCode":"1678B1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1678/problem/B1"}